    "principles": [
      "Box, manual, cartridge, barcode, ROM revision and print revision are separate dimensions.",
      "A cartridge suffix does not automatically define a national packaging market.",
      "A barcode can be shared by several regional packages or markets.",
      "A regional package can contain more than one cartridge/software variant.",
      "A print revision is not a new videogame.",
      "A label suffix such as -1 does not by itself prove ROM revision 1.1.",
      "Current RegionAtlas region is a search hint, never proof.",
      "Observed suffixes such as EUR and EUU are identity/search clues, not universal country maps."
    ]
  },
